{"id":"transit-overtime-against-peers","tier":"REDFLAG","title":"Transit overtime: BART, Golden Gate and Muni against other transit agencies","question":"Do the transit operators that serve San Francisco pay more overtime than other large California transit agencies?","finding":"In 2024 BART paid overtime equal to 16.2% of regular pay, 16,162 dollars per paid position, and 48 positions were paid more in overtime than in regular pay; it ranks 1 of 13 transit payrolls compared. Golden Gate Bridge district: 7.4%. Muni, inside the City payroll: 13.1%. Highest: San Francisco Bay Area Rapid Transit District 16.2%, San Diego Transit Corporation 15.7%, Sacramento Regional Transit System 14.6%.","how":"State Controller raw export. Transit agencies are the special districts with 400 or more paid positions in 2024 whose name says transit, transportation district, rapid, metro, bus or rail; Muni is the City department whose name says municipal transportation. The export does not say whether a year is a calendar or a fiscal year. San Francisco’s overtime here is $480.3 million for 2024; the City’s own payroll file has $468.9 million for fiscal 2024 and $471.0 million for fiscal 2025, so the two sources are close but not the same and are not mixed in any one figure.","limits":"Agencies differ in what they run (rail, buses, bridges, ferries) and in how much maintenance and construction their own staff do. Overtime often covers vacancies. A position is a row, not a person.","columns":[{"k":"employer","t":"Agency","type":"org"},{"k":"year","t":"Year","type":"year"},{"k":"positions","t":"Paid positions","type":"int"},{"k":"otShare","t":"Overtime as share of regular pay","type":"pct"},{"k":"otPer","t":"Overtime per paid position","type":"usd"},{"k":"otherShare","t":"Other pay as share of regular pay","type":"pct"},{"k":"outliers","t":"Positions paid more in overtime than regular pay","type":"int"}],"rows":[{"employer":"San Francisco Bay Area Rapid Transit District","year":2024,"positi